<%#
  Filter the library by file type. Choosing a type switches to a FLAT, whole-library list of it;
  types compose, so "all my STLs and 3MFs" is two choices. Rendered in both modes, so a filter can
  be started from inside a folder (and immediately leaves it — see #index).

  A DROPDOWN OF WHAT THE LIBRARY ACTUALLY HOLDS, NOT A WALL OF WHAT THE VOCABULARY KNOWS. The chip
  row this replaces rendered every extension in `ROLE_BY_EXT` — ~35 chips, most of them types the
  user has never owned — plus a free-text box for the ones it had never heard of. The options here
  come from `FilesController#ext_facets`, so everything offered exists and everything that exists is
  offered, counts included. The free-text box is gone with the wall it stood beside: there is
  nothing left for it to reach.

  TWO CONTROLS, ONE JOB EACH. The select ADDS a type; the chips REMOVE one; "Clear filter" removes
  all. An active type is therefore absent from the select (see ext_facet_groups) — offering it would
  be an option whose selection changes nothing, since `add_ext` unions into `ext`.
%>
<div class="ext-filter">
  <% slots_left = ext_slots_left?(@exts) %>
  <% groups = ext_facet_groups(@ext_facets, @exts) %>

  <%#
    A plain GET form with an inline `onchange`, exactly like the grid's sort form above — no
    Stimulus controller for what a native form already does, and the result is a shareable URL.

    THE PLACEHOLDER IS `disabled`, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THIS A ONE-WAY CONTROL. Left selectable it
    would be an option that submits `add_ext=`, which `compact_blank` drops — the form would post,
    the page would reload, and nothing would change. Clearing is the "Clear filter" link's job.

    IT GOES INERT WHEN THE TYPE SET IS FULL, for the reason `ext_slots_left?` exists: `resolve_exts`
    keeps only the first MAX_EXTS, so with the set full this control would append a value the
    controller then drops. Disabling also keeps the param out of the query string entirely, so there
    is no dropped value to explain afterwards. The sentence is the helper's one string
    (`ext_limit_title`), shared with nothing now but kept there because it is the answer to a
    condition, not to a control.
  %>
  <form method="get" action="<%= files_path %>" class="ext-picker">
    <% if @exts.any? %><input type="hidden" name="ext" value="<%= @exts.join(',') %>"><% end %>
    <% if @q %><input type="hidden" name="q" value="<%= @q %>"><% end %>
    <label class="muted" for="ext-add">Type</label>
    <% if groups.any? %>
      <%# The bare word or nothing, NEVER an interpolated true/false. `disabled` is a BOOLEAN
          attribute: any value at all turns it on, so writing it as disabled="[interpolation]"
          renders disabled="false" and disables the control permanently. (An ERB comment cannot
          show you the wrong spelling, because the closing brace inside it would end the comment
          and print the remainder onto the page — which is exactly what an earlier draft of this
          comment did, invisibly to every assert_select in the suite and glaringly to anyone who
          opened the page.) %>
      <select name="add_ext" id="ext-add" onchange="this.form.requestSubmit()"
              <%= "disabled" unless slots_left %> title="<%= ext_limit_title unless slots_left %>">
        <option value="" disabled selected><%= @exts.any? ? "Add a type…" : "All types" %></option>
        <% groups.each do |label, entries| %>
          <optgroup label="<%= label %>">
            <% entries.each do |ext, count| %>
              <option value="<%= ext %>">.<%= ext %> (<%= number_with_delimiter(count) %>)</option>
            <% end %>
          </optgroup>
        <% end %>
      </select>
      <%# NO SUBMIT BUTTON — and therefore a `<noscript>` one, because `onchange` is the only thing
          that submits this form. Without JavaScript the select would be a control that visibly
          accepts a choice and never acts on it. %>
      <noscript><button type="submit" class="linkbtn">Filter</button></noscript>
    <% else %>
      <%# Not "no types" — an empty library, or one whose every remaining type is already active.
          A select with only a disabled placeholder in it is a control that cannot be used. %>
      <span class="muted" id="ext-add"><%= @exts.any? ? "no other types" : "no files yet" %></span>
    <% end %>
  </form>

  <% if @exts.any? %>
    <%# The active set. aria-current, NOT aria-pressed: these are LINKS (a GET, a shareable URL),
        and aria-pressed is only supported on role=button — on a link it is invalid ARIA a screen
        reader is free to ignore, which would leave the active state announced by nothing but a
        colour. aria-current is valid here and is what the breadcrumb already uses.

        No sort params, for the reason ext_toggle_path gives: the sort lives in a cookie, so pinning
        it here only bakes a stale choice into a URL someone copies. %>
    <span class="ext-active">
      <% @exts.each do |ext| %>
        <%= link_to ext_toggle_path(ext, @exts, q: @q), class: "chip active", "aria-current": "true",
                    title: "Remove .#{ext} from the filter" do %>
          .<%= ext %><span class="chip-x" aria-hidden="true">×</span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to "Clear filter", files_path({ q: @q }.compact), class: "muted clear-filter" %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
</div>
